Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 07:45:09 -0400
Subject: commandbar: actions mode -- Tab, a leading ">", or Shift-Cmd-P lists
 commands

The bar's second mode (docs/features/commandbar.md K8-K17): Tab in the bar,
a leading ">" or Shift-Cmd-P (IDC_STEDDING_COMMAND_PALETTE) turns the rows
into commands -- Stedding's verbs first (Move Tab to <Space>, Pin/Unpin to
This Space, Move Tab to New Folder, Sleep Tab, Clear This Space, Next and
Previous Space, New Space, the three captures, Copy Link, the sidebar, Show
Keyboard Shortcuts, one on/off row per preference and one cycling row per
dropdown), then every visible, enabled item of Chromium's action registry
with its label and chord. Rows fuzzy-match on the label, the chord sits at
the right, Enter runs the row; a preference row keeps the bar open and
re-reads. Cmd-L opens the bar with the page URL selected; Escape leaves
actions mode and a second Escape closes; private and popup windows list
Chromium's actions only; rows without a target are not built.

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 2 (R6-11), the highest-scored idea of the Zen
mods review: one place for every command, reachable from the keyboard.
Removable when: Chromium ships a command palette of its own.
